   "hypothesis": "Trial 1 confirmed the size-ratio rule: when cancelled volume is below the real order, nothing is flagged, but the lift was only 1.11x. This trial checks whether the rule only links cancellations that happen within a short time of the opposite order. Sizes are the same as the built-in spoofer, but each step takes 20-30s instead of 1-3s, so the fakes are cancelled 20-30s after the real order goes up and live 40-60s in total. If the episode window is only a few seconds, I expect no flags, and fakes that sit longer may push the book readers more. Risks: more fakes get hit, and if the window is long it will still flag.",
